---
// /about — see docs/redesign_15-08-2026_PRs/PR-09-about-and-coaching.md §A.
// Word budget is 700-1000 words of narrative prose (checked with the section headings and link
// labels included, all of which sit inside that range) — see IMPLEMENTATION_NOTES.md.
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import Contact from '../components/home/Contact.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import portrait from '../assets/img/CV_picture_PS_square.jpg';
import lastTenPercent from '../assets/img/ProbPose_McLaughlin.png';

const education = (await getCollection('education')).sort(
  (a, b) => a.data.order - b.data.order,
);

const title = 'About — Mira Purkrábek';
const description =
  'The story behind the CV: cybernetics to Porsche to a computer vision PhD at CTU Prague, how I work, teaching, leading a Superliga floorball team, and life away from the screen.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <Section id="top" size="text">
    <div class="about-hero">
      <Image
        src={portrait}
        alt={site.name}
        width={220}
        height={220}
        class="about-hero__portrait"
      />
      <div class="about-hero__text">
        <h1>About</h1>
        <p class="about-hero__lead">
          I'm Mira — a computer vision researcher and engineer, finishing a PhD
          at the Visual Recognition Group, CTU Prague, under Jiří Matas. I'm
          currently a research intern at Qualcomm's XR Labs in Amsterdam,
          working on 3D scene reconstruction and understanding. Across all of
          it, the question I keep coming back to is the same one: how do you
          make computer vision work once the benchmark's clean assumptions stop
          holding — bodies half out of frame, people overlapping in a crowd,
          camera angles nobody trained for.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <Prose>
      <h2 id="story">How I got here</h2>
      <p>
        I started in cybernetics and robotics at CTU, and found computer vision
        through sport — my bachelor's and master's theses tracked floorball
        players across multiple cameras, well before I had a name like "human
        pose estimation" for what I was doing.
      </p>
      <p>
        Then I left research for two years. At Porsche Engineering I wrote
        control-unit software for the Taycan — a car now built more than 170,000
        times over — and later worked across the components of Porsche's High
        Power Charging platform. It's a different kind of rigor when your code
        ships inside a car instead of a paper deadline.
      </p>
      <p>
        I went back to research in 2023 for the PhD I'm doing now — and I chose
        it after knowing what production feels like, not instead of finding out.
        That's shaped how I work more than anything else. Since then: a research
        visit to the University of Tübingen's Real Virtual Humans group (Dec
        2025 – Mar 2026), and now a research internship at Qualcomm's XR Labs in
        Amsterdam (Jun – Dec 2026, current).
      </p>

      <h2 id="how-i-work">How I work</h2>
      <p>A few things guide how I approach a problem:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The last 10% is the interesting part.</strong> Most methods work
          fine on the easy cases; I care about what breaks — keypoints outside the
          image crop (ProbPose), people overlapping in a crowd (BBox-Mask-Pose), camera
          angles nobody trained for (RePoGen).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Evaluate before you model.</strong> You can't fix what you can't
          measure. Several of my contributions are datasets and metrics rather than
          models — CropCOCO, Extended OKS, OCHuman-Pose.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Ship it.</strong> Code, models and demos go public by default. Internal
          tools should get used, not just built — PoseAnnotator started as a lightweight
          pose-annotation tool for one dataset and got reused for several since; Revie
          retrieves a clip from a sports-hall camera system in under half a second
          and is used in real training sessions and matches.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Work with the people using the output.</strong> Police forensics
          analysts, infant-development researchers, floorball coaches — the problem
          looks different from where they stand, and that's usually where the real
          constraint is.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <figure>
        <Image
          src={lastTenPercent}
          alt="Pose estimation overlaid on an athlete whose limbs extend outside the cropped image, with keypoints correctly predicted as out-of-frame."
          width={1200}
          height={652}
          class="about-figure__img"
        />
        <figcaption>
          ProbPose predicting keypoints outside the visible crop — one version
          of "the last 10%."
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h2 id="teaching">Teaching and supervision</h2>
      <p>
        I teach <a
          href="https://cw.fel.cvut.cz/wiki/courses/b4b33rpz/start"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">RPZ — Pattern Recognition and Machine Learning</a
        > at CTU, covering statistical decision theory and classifiers from perceptrons
        to neural nets. Two papers I supervised have turned into real publications:
        SAM-pose2seg, which won Best Student Paper at CVWW 2026, and PC-CSE. I'm open
        to supervising theses and to research discussions. I don't keep fixed consultation
        hours, so reach out in advance.
      </p>

      <h2 id="leadership">Leading a team, off the field</h2>
      <p>
        From 2017 I coached floorball at Sokol Královské Vinohrady, working from
        assistant up to head coach of the men's Superliga team in 2024 — one of
        the youngest head coaches in the league's history at 27. Around 200
        matches, more than 100 of them in the Superliga.
      </p>
      <p>
        None of it was really about floorball. It was making decisions with
        incomplete information under a game clock, giving feedback people could
        actually act on, and building a competitive team around clear roles and
        dedication instead of star names, because SKV never had the budget for
        star names. We still put together the best results in the club's history
        on one of the smallest budgets in the league.
      </p>
      <p>
        I stepped down in summer 2025 to focus on research, and stayed on as a
        consultant. <a href="/coaching">The full story →</a>
      </p>

      <h2 id="personal">Away from work</h2>
      <p>
        Away from a screen, I'm usually in the mountains, travelling, or a few
        chapters into a psychology book or an epic fantasy series — sometimes
        both in the same week.
      </p>

      <h2 id="education">Education</h2>
      <ul>
        {
          education.map((entry) => (
            <li>
              <strong>
                {entry.data.degree} in {entry.data.field}
              </strong>{' '}
              — {entry.data.institution}, {entry.data.period}.
              {entry.data.note && ` ${entry.data.note}`}
              {entry.data.thesisLink && (
                <>
                  {' '}
                  <a
                    href={entry.data.thesisLink}
                    target="_blank"
                    rel="noopener"
                  >
                    Thesis ↗
                  </a>
                </>
              )}
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
    </Prose>
  </Section>

  <Contact />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about-hero {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .about-hero__portrait {
    width: 140px;
    height: 140px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
  }

  :global(.about-figure__img) {
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  }

  .about-hero__text h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }

  .about-hero__lead {
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .about-hero {
      flex-direction: row;
      align-items: center;
    }

    .about-hero__portrait {
      width: 180px;
      height: 180px;
    }
  }
</style>
